{{also|mean time}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|mean time}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|menetime}}, equivalent to {{compound|en|mean|time}}. Adverb is by [[ellipsis]] from {{m|en||in the meantime}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|mēnʹtīm}}, {{IPA|/ˈmiːntaɪm/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-meantime.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[time]] spent [[waiting]] for another event; time in [[between]].
#: ''I'll get started tomorrow but, in the '''meantime''', let's see if we can get a few more opinions.''

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|between-time}}

